sections.body:
- TestReadOnlyAllowlistIncludesGoDoc (`internal/engine`): `LocalReadOnlyAllowlist("/w")` and `CloudUIAllowlist("/w")` each hold `Bash(go doc*)` and the pinned `Bash(go -C /w doc*)`. Together the entries match `go doc ./internal/adjcli Client.Init` and `go -C /w doc ./internal/adjcli Client.Init`. No entry starts with `Bash(go -C *`. Fails first: the entries are missing.
- TestReadOnlyAllowlistRefusesGoWritesEndingInDoc (`internal/engine`): no entry of either list matches any command from `goWritesEndingIn("doc")` (`go -C /w get example.com/m doc`, `go -C /w mod edit -droprequire=x doc`, `go -C /w build -o /w/bin doc`, `go -C /w install example.com/m doc`, `go -C /w generate doc`). No entry matches `go -C /other doc ./x` or `go -C /w/sub doc ./x`. This guards the pinned form: the unpinned `go -C * doc*` would match the write forms.
- TestReadOnlyAllowlistIncludesSlicerRelayRolesShow (`internal/engine`): both lists hold `Bash(slicer relay-roles show*)`, which matches `slicer relay-roles show`, `slicer relay-roles show --json --root /w` and `slicer relay-roles show --root /w`. Fails first: the entry is missing.
- TestReadOnlyAllowlistRefusesRelayRolesWrites (`internal/engine`): no entry of either list matches `slicer relay-roles init`, `slicer relay-roles init --force --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles add r1 --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles set r1 --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles remove r1`, `slicer relay-roles move r1 --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles rule-add --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles rule-edit --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles rule-remove --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles apply --stdin --root /w`, `slicer relay-roles --root /w add r1` or `slicer ai relay-roles --root /w`.
- TestReviewerTempSlicerWritesPinTheRootToTheTempDir (`internal/engine`): with `tmp = "/t/run/reviewer-1"`, `ReviewerTempSlicerWrites(tmp)` has entries that match each of these, with `--root` last: `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer init --force --relay-roles --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer add "x" --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer set S1 --field status=done --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer note S1 --text "x" --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer done S1 --note "x" --root /t/run/reviewer-1` and `slicer relay-roles add r1 --root /t/run/reviewer-1`. Fails first: no function.
- TestReviewerTempSlicerWritesRefuseOtherRoots (`internal/engine`): the list `LocalReadOnlyAllowlist("/w")` plus `ReviewerTempSlicerWrites("/t/run/reviewer-1")` matches none of these:
  - roots other than the temp dir: `slicer init --root /w`, `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-10`, `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-1/sub`, `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-1/../x`, `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-1 --root /w`;
  - a root that is not last: `slicer init --root /t/run/reviewer-1 /w`, `slicer init` and `slicer init --root=/t/run/reviewer-1`;
  - a quoted look-alike: `slicer note S1 --text "--root /t/run/reviewer-1" --root /w` and `slicer note S1 --root /w --text "x --root /t/run/reviewer-1"`;
  - `--root` before the subcommand: `slicer --root /t/run/reviewer-1 init`;
  - subcommands outside the fixed list: `slicer ai relay --init-roles --root /t/run/reviewer-1`, `slicer changelog add S1 --text "x" --root /t/run/reviewer-1`;
  - every command of `TestReadOnlyAllowlistMatchesNoTrackingWrite`'s `writes` list that ends `--root /w`.
- TestReviewerTempSlicerWritesNeedASafeTempDir (`internal/engine`): `ReviewerTempSlicerWrites` returns no entries for `""`, `"t"`, `"rel/t"`, `"/t/../u"`, `"/a b"`, `"/a*b"`, `"/a,b"`, `"/a'b"`, `` `/a"b` ``, `"/a(b"` and `"/a)b"`, as `PinGitC` drops its entries for an unpinnable worktree. Each call returns its own slice.
- TestClaudeRunnerGivesOnlyTheReviewerTheTempSlicerWrites (`internal/daemon`): with the table of `TestClaudeRunnerGivesOnlyTheReviewerATMPDirWriteGrant`, the `claude.Spec` allowlist holds `ReviewerTempSlicerWrites(tmp)` exactly when the role is a reviewer with a process temp dir, on `claude` and `claude-local`. On `claude-local` the approval hook's allowlist holds them too. A gate, an architect, a spec check, a UI pass, and a reviewer without `TMPDir` get none.
